  {
    "episode_id": 45125,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/4/5/45125.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 15,
    "turn_text": "I introduced a piece of legislation that the Democrats objected to that would have broadened the whistleblowers to include all contractors, but also made it retroactive because I think Edward Snowden did a service to the country by revealing that James Clapper was lying. James Clapper said they were not recording all the information with regards to our phone calls. And it turns out he lied. He lied to the Senate. And so it's funny, everybody's all hot and heavy about this impeachment thing, but nobody ever did a thing to James Clapper. He should have gone to jail for what he did. And I think Edward Snowden did a real service to our country by revealing that. And consequently, we actually got rid of that program. We actually, Congress came together, even though they all said they hated Edward Snowden, the information that he brought forward was then used by Congress to reform all of this gathering of information on our phone calls.",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_03",
