    "turn_idx": 24,
    "turn_text": "know, anytime you start messing with what the age of adulthood is, then you have to work with the contradictions of other things. We still have a draft. We don't use it. We have selective service. You have to register. But potentially people could be drafted at 18 again. And I guess my concern is that if you're drafted at 18 and then you can't smoke until you're 21, is that really fair? We had that with voting for a long time. Remember, a lot of the kids that were going to Vietnam weren't allowed to vote, and people are, I think, rightly annoyed that they were being asked to go thousands of miles across the ocean to fight a war, and they weren't allowed to vote. So I think the age of adulthood needs to be the same. Now, if you want to make everything 21, I guess we could do that. My guess is the Democrats don't want to change the voting age from 18 to 21.",
