    "turn_idx": 31,
    "turn_text": "There's all kinds of waste. And so the penny plan but forced government to cut out waste. I also introduced this week and had a vote on a new one called the penny plan for infrastructure. I think whether you're a Republican or a Democrat, a lot of people are interested in trying to keep our roads up to speed and making sure that they're drivable. And the penny plan for infrastructure would take one penny from every other department, make them cut waste, and it would take that money and put it into an infrastructure fund. It'd be about $12 billion a year. It's not enough to fix everything, but it'd do 8 to 10 big road projects or bridge projects. It would do a couple thousand miles of interstate. so it really would be worthwhile we have a vote on that unfortunate we only got about twenty votes for it because most of the people washington are stuck in their ways and they promise you more roads they promise you more money but they never get around the funding it and so it never happens",
